From: Noswad <64293615+TheNoswad@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] clk: samsung: gs101: do not save/restore the MIF mirror queue

samsung_clk_suspend()/resume() write every top_clk_regs register back.
The MIFMIRROR_QUEUE_* block (0x3e00-0x3e30) is the live queue for ACPM's
MIF clock switches: writing MIFMIRROR_QUEUE_BUSY back (even its own
value) takes the SoC down, so deep suspend reset the phone. The vendor
SYS_SLEEP save list does not include these registers. Found by writing
each CMU_TOP register back one at a time; all other gs101 CMU registers
survive the write-back.
---
diff --git a/drivers/clk/samsung/clk-gs101.c b/drivers/clk/samsung/clk-gs101.c
index 12a867e99..dc522df4a 100644
--- a/drivers/clk/samsung/clk-gs101.c
+++ b/drivers/clk/samsung/clk-gs101.c
@@ -622,16 +622,11 @@ static const unsigned long top_clk_regs[] __initconst = {
 	QUEUE_ENTRY5_BLK_CMU_CMU_TOP,
 	QUEUE_ENTRY6_BLK_CMU_CMU_TOP,
 	QUEUE_ENTRY7_BLK_CMU_CMU_TOP,
-	MIFMIRROR_QUEUE_CTRL_REG,
-	MIFMIRROR_QUEUE_ENTRY0,
-	MIFMIRROR_QUEUE_ENTRY1,
-	MIFMIRROR_QUEUE_ENTRY2,
-	MIFMIRROR_QUEUE_ENTRY3,
-	MIFMIRROR_QUEUE_ENTRY4,
-	MIFMIRROR_QUEUE_ENTRY5,
-	MIFMIRROR_QUEUE_ENTRY6,
-	MIFMIRROR_QUEUE_ENTRY7,
-	MIFMIRROR_QUEUE_BUSY,
+	/*
+	 * Local: not MIFMIRROR_QUEUE_* (0x3e00-0x3e30). That queue mirrors the
+	 * ACPM-driven MIF clock switches; writing QUEUE_BUSY back from the
+	 * syscore save/restore kills the SoC (vendor SYS_SLEEP never saves it).
+	 */
 	GENERALIO_ACD_CHANNEL_0,
 	GENERALIO_ACD_CHANNEL_1,
 	GENERALIO_ACD_CHANNEL_2,
